to say ResolveEvent Second Chance:
	say "     Meandering about the broken cross street, you catch sight of a slight shimmer of magenta light flashing through the shadows of a nearby storm drain. Unnerved, you feel your hackles rise at the sudden thought the odd ooze might be tailing you, and quickly drop down to all fours. Ready howl at them the moment your eyes meet, yet as you tilt your snoot toward the opening, you let out a chuffed guffaw as your gaze is greeted by deflating metallic pink balloon bobbing along its ceiling. Guess the goo was true to its word, you shrug ambling to your feet with a playful shake of your head. Off handedly though, a private part of you chaffs at the gels absence, why you can't be certain, be it curiosity, lascivious impulses, a desire to be fawned over, or some taint instinct tickles at the back of your mind urging you to cry out their name. If nothing else you might at least learn more about them and your cuddly body. You muse, absentmindedly patting your milfy curves.";
	LineBreak;
	say "     [bold type]Do you call out to them[roman type]?";
	LineBreak;
	say "     [italic type]Author's Note: Choosing not to ends this story, no new content will ever be unlocked for this path, nor shall you be able to access any of this infection's special features. Additionally, you will not be offered this chance again, or receive any rewards for refusing to call out to them[roman type].";
	let End_of_the_line_Choices be a list of text;
	add "Don't call them?" to End_of_the_line_Choices;
	add "Call them?" to End_of_the_line_Choices;
	let End_of_the_line_Choice be what the player chooses from End_of_the_line_Choices;
	if End_of_the_line_Choice is: 
		-- "Don't call them?":
			say "     Gah, this is stupid,what in the heck are you even doing? You grumble under your breath with an annoyed shake of your head, quietly cursing what nanite tinted madness would make you miss that creepy gel. No matter, for better or worse, you're finally free of them, and if nothing else, you still have your matronly body to enjoy. True, some wary side of you ruminates, it might be hard to maintain your infection with a consistent source of foxy nanites, yet that's a bridge you can cross later. For now, you make a mental note to milk yourself and paw off as you can, or maybe invest in a nanite collector. Still, that's a problem for future [name of player] to deal with, you shrug, as you amble along, more than content to put this strange chapter of your post apocalyptic life behind you.";
			LineBreak;
			say "    [bold type]Thanks for playing: Snuggle Fox content end here[roman type].";
		-- "Call them?":
			say "     Yielding to your baser urges, you take a deep breath, and hold it for just a spell, mentally weighing the dangers of calling out to this gel, against the sweetness of its offer and the blissful memories of your brief time with the aberrant creature. As these feeling war within you, you can sense a tightness building in your breast with each passing second, before you whisper the creature's name with an almost defeated hiss, 'Snuggle'. Unsure what to expect, the word seems to echo about the vacant streets, distorting and warping with flickering recitation as it ripples outward. Till at last it peters out, and the area goes deathly quiet like before, as you simply shrug and begin plodding onward, ready to go about your day once. Yet as you take your first shuffling steps, a subtle metal rattle coming from a nearby manhole. Turning to face it, your eyes go wide as magenta ooze pools about its edges, in a bubbling froth of shimmering slim. Sn-snuggle? You peep, voice laced with a nibbling worry while the asphalt beneath your dainty paws trembles at the ooze's intuition.";
			say "     Taking a set back, your eyes go wide as the cover is violently tossed off skyward by the vast upwell of scintillating gel while the pavement cracks and quaking rubble dances about your talons as the eruption flares ever higher. Casting a growing shadow over you, and the burned wreck populating the area, nearing the upper stories of the nearby build though. The gel curves towards you like a serpent waiting to stroke as worry alloyed alarm flares through you as you take set in base fear of what you just unleashed. Yet, no sooner do you take your first step back does a single elated girly voice cry out in triumph, 'PET!' as the morphic spire of metallic slime surges toward you. Billowing and twisting like a living riptide, its tips bulge outward into the familiar shape of the shifty vixen. Its arms outstretched and eyes gleaming like searchlights in the dark while it cascades over you as it sweeps you off your feet, 'Oh precious Pet we knew you'd come around!' The gel cries, lovingly nuzzling its supple cheeks against as it body settles about you.";
